<title>NEW ZEALAND: Lightning disrupts Auckland power supply.</title>
<headline>Lightning disrupts Auckland power supply.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lightning struck a transmission line in the Bombay Hills early on Friday morning, knocking out power supply to much of Auckland, Trans Power said.</p>
<p>The line supplies power from the Huntly Power Station to Henderson and north of the Auckland Harbour Bridge.</p>
<p>The strike caused an overload on the remaining line at 7.16 a.m., wiping out supply to north of Auckland and to some parts of Auckland city. Power was restored by 8.04 a.m.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
